{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And this is the law of the sacrifice of peace-offerings.</b> This offering is of two kinds: the todah (thanksgiving) and the shelamim (peace-offerings). With the todah offering one would bring bread — unleavened and leavened — and there were forty loaves: ten of unleavened bread and ten of leavened, ten of wafers and ten of boiled cakes. This is as written: ״והקריב על זבח התודה חלות מצות בלולות בשמן ורקיקי מצות משוחים בשמן וסולת מרובכת חלות בלולות בשמן״ — and afterward it says: ״על חלות לחם חמץ יקריב קרבנו״ — behold, four kinds. And Scripture says: ״והקריב ממנו אחד מכל קרבן תרומה לה׳״ — this explains that from these three kinds he takes one from each and every one of them as a terumah (heave-offering), that is, the tithe. This is like the terumat ma'aser (tithe-offering) that the Levite gives to the priest — a tithe of the tithe, called terumat ma'aser. If so, there are thirty unleavened cakes and ten leavened. And the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted that the weight of the ten leavened loaves equals the weight of the thirty unleavened, and so it appears from the verse, which divided them, and the language proves it — for it mentions ״חלות מצות בלולות בשמן״ and ״רקיקי מצות משוחים בשמן״ and ״סלת מרבכת חלות בלולות בשמן״, thereby informing us of their equivalence, that each kind is ten; and afterward it mentions ״על חלות לחם חמץ יקריב קרבנו״. And the shelamim offering does not come for thanksgiving; it is a vow or a freewill offering, as it is written: ״ואם נדר או נדבה זבח קרבנו״, and the one who brings it is not obligated to bring bread. And as for the fact that he would bring leavened bread in the todah offering — but did not the Torah say (Leviticus 2:11) ״כי כל שאור וכל דבש לא תקטירו״? Rather, the matter is that it was not offered upon the altar, and the intent concerning it is not for an offering but only for waving (tenufah)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:23:49.064808041Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}